@startuml weather_zip_block
title Weather by zip code: OpenAI Agents SDK governed by K9-AIF
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Web page or CLI\n(zip code, role)" as Client

rectangle "K9-AIF Router\n(in a deployed app: event_type weather.lookup over Kafka)" as Router #line.dashed

rectangle "OpenAI path" as OAI {
  rectangle "WeatherZipOrchestrator\nOpenAIAgentsOrchestratorAdapter\n(is an Orchestrator)" as Adapter
  rectangle "OpenAI Agents SDK Runner" as Runner
  rectangle "WeatherAgent\n(agents/yaml/weather_agent.yaml)" as Agent
}

rectangle "Shared K9-AIF services (config/config.yaml)" as Shared {
  rectangle "Zero Trust\n(role policy: customer, staff)" as ZT
  rectangle "k9x Shield\n(ingress, tool calls, tool results,\nevery reply, final answer)" as Shield
  rectangle "K9 Model Router\n(task 'weather', tool_calling required)" as MR
}

rectangle "Ollama, OpenAI-compatible API\nlocal_tools: qwen2.5:7b (tool_calling)\nlocal_tiny: llama3.2:1b (not eligible)" as Models

rectangle "Tools" as T {
  rectangle "lookup_zip" as LZ
  rectangle "current_weather" as CW
}

rectangle "api.zippopotam.us\n(zip -> place, coordinates)" as Zip
rectangle "api.open-meteo.com\n(coordinates -> weather)" as Meteo

Client --> Adapter : this example:\ndirect call
Client ..> Router : deployed app
Router ..> Adapter

Adapter --> Runner : run()
Runner --> Agent

Adapter ..> ZT : run: action weather.lookup
Agent ..> ZT : each turn: openai_agent:WeatherAgent
Adapter ..> Shield : request, final answer
Agent ..> Shield : every tool call, result, reply
Agent ..> MR : every model call
MR --> Models

Agent --> LZ
Agent --> CW
LZ --> Zip
CW --> Zip
CW --> Meteo

note right of T
  current_weather takes the zip code and
  looks the coordinates up itself: a tool
  never runs on a value the model supplies
  when the system of record has it.
end note
@enduml
